// Minimal inference path over the real production model.
//
// This test was written against an API that never existed:
//   gguf_dequant_q4km(raw, n) -> pointer to an f32 buffer
// lib/std/gguf.quanta instead exposes dequant_q4k(raw, nelements, out) writing
// f64 (8-byte) values into a caller-supplied buffer. The old test also fed
// gguf_softmax a 12-byte buffer for 3 f64 values, and asserted nothing -- it
// printed "Expected: y[0]=17 y[1]=39" as a literal string rather than
// comparing. Both are fixed here: the real API is called, and every result is
// compared against an authoritative value with a non-zero exit on mismatch.
//
// Element width is f64 (8 bytes) throughout, matching gguf_softmax and
// dequant_q4k. The Q4_K reference bits below are the true decoded values of
// super-block 0 of blk.0.ffn_gate.weight in
// QUANTA-LFM2.5-2.6Bv1-Q4_K_M.gguf, independently computed from the layout in
// ggml-quants.c dequantize_row_q4_K / get_scale_min_k4.

import std/fs
import std/gguf

